	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: ["4D54B17785EC3EC0"]
			description: [
				"The Volitans is a highly territorial semi-aquatic dragon species adapted for environmental control, area denial, and prolonged territorial occupation. Volitans individuals are known for gradually altering surrounding environments through the accumulation of toxins and venomous biological residue. Volitans pursue prey over long distances. And they also establish dominance by controlling movement within their territory, forcing intruders into increasingly hazardous conditions through toxic spines, lingering breath attacks, and environmental pressure. Although often associated with toxicity, Volitans' activity is not inherently destructive. Once territorial disturbances cease, affected ecosystems frequently stabilize over time, suggesting the species alters environments as a defensive adaptation rather than out of indiscriminate aggression. &n&4If met in the wild, it will view a person as hostile.&r"
				"Before a Volitans can be tamed, &4&nit must first be subdued in combat&r. Wild Volitans become vulnerable only after their health is &4&nreduced to approximately 60 HP&r, causing the dragon to enter a stunned state. Once stunned, the dragon may be fed preferred foods such as &n&4tropical fish, pufferfish, raw cod, salmon, and Hearty Dragon Meal&r."
				"Feeding a Volitans does not guarantee successful taming. Failed attempts will restore a portion of the dragon's health, immediately ending its stunned state and forcing the player to subdue it again."
				"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/volitans.png width:300 height:150 align:center}"
			]
			id: "7CD9757E1CD48E5A"
			rewards: [
				{
					amount: 70L
					currency: "eternalcurrencies:ancientcoins"
					id: "1D5F754628A99ADC"
